    "license": "Original project-authored floor supports. Complete original project-authored wall mirror models retained from precisely pinned local resources. No external model or texture. Three.js 0.187.0 is MIT licensed, copyright 2010–2026 three.js authors, with the pinned local LICENSE retained.",
    "prompt": "Purpose: project-authored free-standing floor mirrors with four real mirror contours, complete wall-mirror frame assemblies and connected physical floor supports. Specification: fixed total envelope .80m x 1.80m x .60m, bottom-centred origin, metres, +Y up and +Z forward. Installation: floor-surface in room/area, identity instance scale, fixed blocking footprint .80m x .60m and empty state/use points. Mirror contract: planar-mirror-v1 / single-512-v1 with face at [0,.92,.026], actual mirror-surface/back/base/post nodes, one coplanar face mesh and one runtime reflection target. Geometry: import the exact original wall GLB, bake +.92m into each Y vertex in Float32, retain original triangle topology and all frame/back/mullion geometry, keep every node identity and shift declared convex contours to the identical final Float32 coordinates. Supports: grounded closed .24 x .06 x .38 base, closed .08 x .52 x .04 post, actual positive-volume contact into convex thick backing, plus distinct solid low support feet. Production: editable parameters, exact source/contract/generator/model SHA256 pins, deterministic CPU GLTFExporter and actual GLTFLoader readback. No baked reflection image, new light, new clock, moving support or physics simulation. Actual host-scene reflection continues through the existing shared runtime. Support design: The original .70m circular mirror and brass ring above a connected broad low plinth.",
